<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Makhanda (prophet)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1820">1820</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Nxele, Makana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makhanda">Makhanda</a>, also called Nxele, was a Xhosa prophet and war leader. In the Fifth Frontier War he led an assault by some 10,000 Xhosa on the British garrison at Grahamstown on 22 April 1819, which was repulsed. He surrendered and was imprisoned on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robben-island">Robben Island</a>, and drowned in 1820 while escaping. The city of Grahamstown was renamed Makhanda in his honour in 2018.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/makhanda-prophet.jpg" alt="Makhanda (prophet)" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thembani Onceya · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Makhanda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
